WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:05.880
Denise Richards burst onto the scene with a steamy&nbsp;
kiss in "Wild Things" — but it wouldn't be the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:11.580
last time she attracted attention! From late-'90s&nbsp;
"It" girl to OnlyFans star, the Real Housewife&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:17.520
has always managed to keep things interesting.
 
In 1998, Denise Richards starred in the sleazy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:22.680
classic "Wild Things." Her three-way kiss with&nbsp;
Neve Campbell and Matt Dillon was a prominent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:27.480
draw for audiences, but the film holds other&nbsp;
twists and delights besides all the smooching.

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:32.880
Richards played Kelly Van Ryan in the film, a&nbsp;
wealthy and popular girl who accuses guidance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:38.820
counselor Sam Lombardo of statutory rape. The two&nbsp;
girls admit to falsifying their accusations on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:43.980
the stand, which prompts Lombardo to sue Kelly's&nbsp;
family for a significant chunk of change. From&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:49.080
there, things get twistier and twistier. Everyone&nbsp;
is an accomplice on the grift, and everyone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:55.980
backstabs everyone else. It's high melodrama.
 
In 1999, Denise Richards co-starred opposite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.980 --> 00:01:00.660
Kirstie Alley in "Drop Dead Gorgeous." The&nbsp;
deadpan mockumentary was about a small-town&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:04.800
beauty pageant and the series of horrific&nbsp;
murders committed in pursuit of its crown.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:09.420
The film is now considered a cult classic&nbsp;
but was underseen upon initial release.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:14.460
Richards played Becky Leeman, the presumed&nbsp;
favorite in the teen beauty pageant contest.

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:19.080
"Oh, my god. Lights, camera and&nbsp;
me without a stitch of makeup on."

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:24.840
Unfortunately for Richards, 1999 was also&nbsp;
the year she co-starred in "The World is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:29.220
Not Enough," starring Pierce Brosnan&nbsp;
as James Bond. Richards played nuclear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:33.660
physicist Christmas Jones in the film,&nbsp;
but her role was universally panned by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:37.920
critics. Yahoo!'s James Bond blog even&nbsp;
had this to say about Richards' part:

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:41.820
"Look up any poll or column from recent&nbsp;
years on the worst Bond girls ever,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:44.820
and Dr. Christmas Jones comes up every time."

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:47.580
Dr. Christmas Jones came to represent all the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:50.760
cheese that made Bond fans&nbsp;
sour on the Brosnan films.

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:54.180
"I thought Christmas only comes once a year."

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:57.480
So, in a way, Denise Richards&nbsp;
is partially to thank for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.480 --> 00:01:59.820
grittier Daniel Craig version of the character.

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:05.580
During the 2000s and early 2010s, Denise&nbsp;
Richards' film career kind of puttered out.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:11.100
Her biggest roles post-Bond were mostly cameos in&nbsp;
prominent films. People remember her 10 seconds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:15.420
in "Love Actually" better than her starring role&nbsp;
in "Deep in the Valley." At the very end of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:20.160
Christmas classic, Richards' character travels&nbsp;
to England to meet sad sack Colin's best friend.

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:24.720
However, one of her most memorable guest&nbsp;
appearances was on a controversial seventh&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:27.780
season episode of "Friends," in&nbsp;
which she played Cassie Gellar.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:31.740
This episode crossed a major line for&nbsp;
many "Friends" fans when Ross tried&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:35.520
to kiss Cassie. Ross even had this&nbsp;
lame explanation for his actions:

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:38.460
"I haven't had sex in a very long time."

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:42.300
Grantland's Sam Hockley-Smith even cites&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:44.400
the episode as the one where&nbsp;
the show jumped the shark.  

00:02:45.551 --> 00:02:51.120
In 2002, Richards married Charlie Sheen. Their&nbsp;
courtship started normally enough, but things took&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:55.800
a turn shortly after Richards became pregnant&nbsp;
with the couple's second daughter, Lola Rose&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.800 --> 00:03:01.860
Sheen. In 2005, Richards separated from Sheen,&nbsp;
while she was still pregnant with Lola. She later&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:06.360
sought a restraining order against him, citing&nbsp;
threats he'd allegedly made against her life.

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:11.160
Richards found ways to parlay her fracturing&nbsp;
personal life into work by starring in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:16.920
reality show "Denise Richards: It's Complicated"&nbsp;
in 2008 and publishing her memoir in 2011.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:21.900
In the memoir, she talks about Sheen's sudden&nbsp;
transformation into someone she did not trust.

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:25.980
"Yeah, I am on a drug, it's called Charlie Sheen!"

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:27.360
She told the Huffington Post,

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:30.480
"The man I fell in love with&nbsp;
is very compassionate, humble,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:35.040
has a wonderful heart. And the behavior that&nbsp;
a lot of us saw in the last six months is not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:40.320
the person that I met and fell in love with."
 
In 2018, Richards joined the cast of the "The Real&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:44.580
Housewives of Beverly Hills." Richards&nbsp;
was on all of season 9 but left season&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:48.240
10 prematurely after Brandi Glanville&nbsp;
asserted that the two had hooked up.

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:53.580
When Richards refused to return for Season&nbsp;
11, no one was very surprised. The show's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:59.220
executive producer Andy Cohen told People the&nbsp;
negotiations broke down over pay, but Richards&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.220 --> 00:04:03.540
said that she wanted to spend time with people&nbsp;
that actually liked her. A source told People:

00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:08.580
"She was looking to replace RHOBH&nbsp;
with time loving her amazing husband,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.580 --> 00:04:11.580
children and who knows, maybe even friends now." 
 &nbsp;

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:16.500
In addition to her acting career, Denise&nbsp;
Richards is also an accomplished model.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:20.940
She started modeling as a teenager and was&nbsp;
successful enough to travel the world for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:25.800
photoshoots and commercials. Once her acting&nbsp;
career took off, she spent less time modeling,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:31.260
but still made time to pose in the Gala&nbsp;
Christmas issue of "Playboy" magazine in 2004.

00:04:31.260 --> 00:04:33.480
Richards had given birth to her oldest daughter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:37.740
Sami, just months before the photoshoot.&nbsp;
Her husband at the time, Charlie Sheen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.740 --> 00:04:41.640
was a "Playboy" fan and encouraged&nbsp;
her to be in the magazine — but she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:45.840
had her own reasons for doing it as well.&nbsp;
Richards revealed to Us Weekly in 2011:

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:51.000
"I wanted to encourage women that it's OK to&nbsp;
embrace your sexuality even though you're a mom."

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:56.400
Richards has gone through so many highs and lows&nbsp;
that it's hard to keep up with it all. Luckily&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.400 --> 00:05:00.960
for her fans, she released her memoir "The Real&nbsp;
Girl Next Door," which ended up becoming a New&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:05.700
York Times bestseller. The book dives into topics&nbsp;
like her tumultuous marriage with Charlie Sheen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:10.560
the moment she realized they needed a divorce,&nbsp;
and adjusting to life as a single mom. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:13.800
she has insisted that the book&nbsp;
isn't meant to bash her ex-husband,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:18.000
and it doesn't reveal the most private&nbsp;
details of her life. She told Radar Online:

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:22.200
"I went through a whole lot and I get asked a&nbsp;
lot of questions about that time in my life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:26.460
so I figured I would write my story and&nbsp;
hopefully anyone that has been, you know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:30.000
dealing with challenges will know that&nbsp;
there is light at the end of the tunnel."
 &nbsp;

00:05:30.540 --> 00:05:35.700
Richards adopted her daughter Eloise in&nbsp;
2011 and began raising her as a single&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.700 --> 00:05:40.500
mom. But things changed when Richards&nbsp;
tied the knot with Aaron Phypers in 2018.

00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:41.640
"We just got married."
"We're married."

00:05:42.420 --> 00:05:45.660
He began helping Richards&nbsp;
raise her three daughters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:48.000
and adopted Eloise when she was 7 years old.

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:54.180
Eloise has had some developmental delays due to a&nbsp;
rare disorder known as Chromosome 8, Monosomy 8p,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.180 --> 00:05:58.680
which is characterized by a partial deletion&nbsp;
of the eighth chromosome. Richards discovered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.680 --> 00:06:02.520
the news after she noticed Eloise wasn't&nbsp;
reaching milestones at the typical rate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.520 --> 00:06:06.780
such as learning how to walk and talk.&nbsp;
During an emotional reunion on "The Real&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.780 --> 00:06:10.620
Housewives of Beverly Hills," Richards&nbsp;
said that the diagnosis was hard on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.620 --> 00:06:15.000
family. Despite the challenges that come&nbsp;
with this disorder, Richards and Phypers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:18.900
have remained committed to finding the best&nbsp;
medical care for Eloise no matter what.
 &nbsp;

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:24.780
Part of Richards' transformation over the years&nbsp;
has been a result of plastic surgery and cosmetic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:29.220
procedures. In her memoir, she explained that&nbsp;
she's had four breast augmentation surgeries.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.220 --> 00:06:34.260
Richards added that she got her first surgery at&nbsp;
just 19 years old because she thought her A-cup&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:38.700
breasts weren't big enough for Hollywood. She was&nbsp;
in such a rush to get the surgery that she didn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.700 --> 00:06:43.560
properly research doctors, and unfortunately, she&nbsp;
ended up with bigger implants than she wanted.

00:06:43.560 --> 00:06:48.120
The second surgery was meant to reduce her&nbsp;
breast size, but the doctor went against her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.120 --> 00:06:52.980
wishes and gave her even bigger implants. The&nbsp;
third surgery finally reduced her breast size,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.980 --> 00:06:55.920
and the fourth replaced the&nbsp;
implants after they ruptured.

00:06:55.920 --> 00:07:00.600
She has also tried Botox, saying she loved&nbsp;
how the results looked but didn't like the way&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:05.160
they made her face feel. Since then, Richards&nbsp;
has been avoiding Botox and fillers. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.160 --> 00:07:08.100
she has claimed that she's never&nbsp;
used fillers. Some people thought&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.100 --> 00:07:12.660
she did in 2019, but she says she just&nbsp;
gained weight due to a thyroid issue.
 &nbsp;

00:07:13.440 --> 00:07:18.300
So, how does Richards maintain her youthful&nbsp;
appearance without Botox and fillers? It's simple:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.300 --> 00:07:23.280
She takes great care of her skin. Her passion&nbsp;
for skincare led her to create CBme Beauty,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.280 --> 00:07:29.220
a line of hemp-infused skincare products. In a&nbsp;
2020 interview with Us Weekly, Richards explained:

00:07:29.220 --> 00:07:32.640
"I'm in front of the camera so I do&nbsp;
want to take very good care of my skin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:36.540
and that's also why I thought it would be a&nbsp;
great time to venture to have my own skin line."

00:07:36.540 --> 00:07:39.120
The skincare line consists of six products,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:44.460
including a hydrating cream moisturizer and eye&nbsp;
cream. Richards' personal favorite, she said,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.460 --> 00:07:49.080
is the hydrating moisturizer made with&nbsp;
hemp oil. In her interview with Us Weekly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.080 --> 00:07:54.540
she said she plans to expand the line with new&nbsp;
products that contain CBD and other cannabinoids.

00:07:55.080 --> 00:08:00.840
In 2022, Sheen and Richards' then-18-year-old&nbsp;
daughter Sami joined OnlyFans, a site that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.840 --> 00:08:04.080
allows users to sell nude photos&nbsp;
and videos to their subscribers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:07.560
Richards thought it was unfair that&nbsp;
Sami was getting so much backlash,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.560 --> 00:08:10.980
so a week later, she joined the site&nbsp;
as well to support her daughter.

00:08:10.980 --> 00:08:13.560
"I always think it's good&nbsp;
for kids to have a passion."

00:08:13.560 --> 00:08:17.640
Sheen, on the other hand, was very opposed&nbsp;
to his daughter joining OnlyFans. He even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.640 --> 00:08:21.120
blamed Richards for Sami's actions since&nbsp;
they were living together at the time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:25.440
Richards said that all she could do was try&nbsp;
to guide Sami, but at the end of the day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:30.480
she makes her own decisions. On a more positive&nbsp;
note, Richards said during a 2022 interview with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:35.100
the radio show "Jeff Lewis Live" that making an&nbsp;
OnlyFans account has been very lucrative for her.

00:08:35.100 --> 00:08:36.660
"So you were shocked when you got&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.660 --> 00:08:37.380
your first check?"
"I was shocked."

00:08:37.380 --> 00:08:40.620
She posts content that's a bit more&nbsp;
revealing than what she can post on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:45.360
Instagram and said she has full ownership of&nbsp;
what she shares, which she finds empowering.
 &nbsp;

00:08:45.360 --> 00:08:51.180
Richards has helped many charities over the&nbsp;
years. In 2006, she did a nude photoshoot for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.180 --> 00:08:55.080
"Jane" magazine to support the Clothes Off&nbsp;
Our Back Foundation, which helps children&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.080 --> 00:08:59.280
all around the world live better lives. She&nbsp;
collaborated with ShoeDazzle multiple times&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.280 --> 00:09:03.900
in 2012 to design high heels and raise&nbsp;
money for the Kidney Cancer Association,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.900 --> 00:09:07.440
successfully raising over $15,000 in the process.

00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:12.480
She has also been a huge supporter of Best&nbsp;
Friends Animal Society, fostering kittens with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:17.040
the help of her daughters and raising awareness&nbsp;
about the benefits of adopting animals. She even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.040 --> 00:09:21.540
paid for several rescue dogs' medical care,&nbsp;
nursed them back to health, and adopted them.

00:09:22.140 --> 00:09:26.340
Richards stayed busy after leaving "The&nbsp;
Real Housewives of Beverly Hills" in 2020,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.340 --> 00:09:31.980
landing many different roles on TV shows. Perhaps&nbsp;
most notably, she played fun single mom Shauna&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.980 --> 00:09:37.080
Fulton on "The Bold and the Beautiful" for several&nbsp;
years. In the series "Paper Empire," she portrays&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.080 --> 00:09:40.860
a wealthy woman whose opulent lifestyle&nbsp;
gets turned upside-down when her husband&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.860 --> 00:09:46.800
gets arrested. The show is set to premiere&nbsp;
in 2024. Richards also portrayed CIA agent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.800 --> 00:09:52.020
Laura Louis in "The Guardians of Justice."
 
Fans were disappointed when Denise Richards&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.020 --> 00:09:56.400
left "The Real Housewives of Beverly Hills" in&nbsp;
Season 10, but she's officially returning to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.400 --> 00:10:01.560
show for Season 13. Her return was so unexpected&nbsp;
that even the production crew didn't know about it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.560 --> 00:10:05.700
until it happened. Richards randomly showed up&nbsp;
at a screening because she's friends with Real&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:10.080
Housewife Garcelle Beauvais, and then the crew&nbsp;
asked her to attend some events. From there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:13.800
she started getting more involved.&nbsp;
Richards told Variety in 2023:

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:17.040
"I have filmed some episodes&nbsp;
and it's been fun. And you know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.040 --> 00:10:21.180
I'm a big fan of the show, so it was fun to&nbsp;
go back and film a lot of stuff with them."

00:10:21.180 --> 00:10:24.900
Richards has confirmed that she&nbsp;
won't be in Season 13's promo shots,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.900 --> 00:10:28.680
so it seems like she'll be returning as&nbsp;
a guest. There was a lot of drama and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.680 --> 00:10:33.300
negativity surrounding Richards' exit from&nbsp;
the show in 2020, but she says things were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.300 --> 00:10:37.260
different this time around. She told Variety&nbsp;
that she didn't get caught up in the drama&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:37.260 --> 00:10:41.040
and had fun with the whole experience&nbsp;
rather than letting others get her down.

